        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "You\u2019re thinking of a super simple **homemade chocolate / \u201cfat bomb\u201d style candy** using cacao powder, oil, and stevia. Here\u2019s a clean, reliable version with good texture and taste:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf6b Basic Cacao Oil Candy (Sugar-Free)\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"homemade chocolate silicone molds cacao coconut oil\",\"mixing cacao powder coconut oil bowl\",\"pouring chocolate into silicone molds keto candy\",\"finished homemade chocolate squares silicone mold\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n#### Ingredients:\n- \u00bd cup **coconut oil** (melted)  \n- \u00bd cup **unsweetened cacao powder**  \n- 1\u20132 tsp **stevia** (adjust to taste depending on strength)  \n- 1 tsp **vanilla extract** (optional but highly recommended)  \n- Pinch of **sea salt** (optional, enhances flavor)\n\n---\n\n### Instructions:\n1. **Melt the oil**  \n   Gently melt the coconut oil until fully liquid (microwave or stovetop).\n\n2. **Mix everything**  \n   Whisk in cacao powder until smooth.  \n   Add stevia, vanilla, and salt. Taste and adjust sweetness.\n\n3. **Pour into molds**  \n   Pour mixture into silicone molds (or a lined tray if you don\u2019t have molds).\n\n4. **Chill**  \n   Place in the fridge or freezer for 20\u201330 minutes until solid.\n\n5. **Pop out & enjoy**  \n   Keep stored in the fridge because coconut oil melts easily.\n\n---\n\n### Pro Tips:\n- If it tastes **too bitter**, add a little more sweetener or a splash of heavy cream.\n- If it\u2019s **too soft**, increase cacao powder slightly.\n- You can add:\n  - Crushed nuts  \n  - Peanut butter swirl  \n  - Coconut flakes  \n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can give you a version that tastes closer to a **Reese\u2019s cup** or a **fudge texture**."
          ]
        },
